#: sdlc/processes/cache.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run `bun run cat cache:plan <target>`. For each `cache` node it decides NEEDED (derived: the target's recorded read set, from the CI cone and the writer cone, touches what the node `materializes`, plus the `needs` closure), FRESH or STALE (the node's key against the key today's inputs imply; undetermined counts as stale), and so restore, refresh or skip. `nothing needed` when the plan needs no node, when the target has no recorded read set (it could not be derived: the safe direction is to build), when the consumer does not call this process, cannot reach a store, or is told not to (a forced cold run). Skipping is ALWAYS correct: every component's miss path is the consumer building what it needs, so a skip costs time and never correctness."
msgstr ""

